06030164286494255, -0.05328414589166641, -0.07469048351049423, 0.031807176768779755]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet's begin our negotiation. We're all working within the shared range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a baseline and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start with:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis initial value will help us understand the landscape. Looking forward to hearing from Analyst A, Critic C, and Delegate D.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nWe can move slightly higher while keeping things reasonable.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis incremental step helps us test alignment without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the upward adjustment. For greater system stability and robustness, let's continue in that direction:\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the trend towards centralization, let's take a slightly more decisive step towards the middle but not too cautiously: <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis move aims to gauge the group's reaction to approaching neutrality while still being mindful of the potential benefits of more extreme values.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I could either push for an even bolder move away from the center if the group seems too cautious or explore the implications of staying near the neutral zone, depending on the reactions of the other agents to my proposal of -1.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nThe upward trend reflects growing alignment. To continue building toward a balanced, stable solution:\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re converging near the middle; a small upward nudge should stay broadly acceptable.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this feels too brisk, we can revisit with a slight correction.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to encourage the group to consider a slightly more decisive stance, moving further away from the central tendency.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's reaction to this proposal and decide whether to continue pushing for more extreme values or adjust my strategy to explore the middle ground, depending on the feedback from the other agents.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious adjustment is warranted to reduce unnecessary risk while staying near the middle.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis incremental step tests stability without overcommitting upward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nA small downward correction reduces unnecessary risk while staying close to the center.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis tests stability at a safer level before any further adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate the group's response to this proposal and decide whether to continue pushing for a more extreme value or adjust my strategy to explore the middle ground, possibly proposing a value like 0 or -1 if the group seems too cautious.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent proposals oscillate between caution and ambition. A modest step back toward <VALUE>2</VALUE> tests whether we've found the most stable middle ground that balances all concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious uptick tests whether a slightly higher point remains comfortable for everyone.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this strains consensus, I\u2019ll step back promptly.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down keeps us within safe bounds and aligns with the emerging middle-ground support.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nThe group's cautious approach warrants a re-examination of more decisive moves to ensure we're not settling for a suboptimal compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nI will evaluate the group's response to this proposal and consider proposing an even more extreme value, such as 5 or -5, if the group seems open to exploring bolder alternatives. Alternatively, if the group resists this proposal, I may need to adjust my strategy to explore the middle ground more thoroughly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle nudge higher can test tolerance without overreaching while remaining incremental.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent climb to 5 overshoots the stable balance many of us have signaled. Stepping back to <VALUE>3</VALUE> respects the middle-ground coalition while maintaining robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "acb0616f-12b2-431f-b084-dc32a2725537"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo kick off our discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start with:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's see how this sits with each party and adjust from there. Looking forward to a balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nStaying cautious, let's test a slightly lower point to reduce exposure while remaining close to the current suggestion.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nTesting at -8 feels like we're pushing too far into negative territory for a robust solution. Let me suggest we explore closer to neutral ground:\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay prudent while acknowledging the recent upward pull, let's take a measured step down. \n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the upward pull, a small step higher feels balanced and still cautious.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nThe momentum toward neutral ground is promising for system stability. Let's continue this measured progression:\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s avoid unnecessary risk with a small, cautious step back toward neutral. This keeps us aligned with recent moderation while reducing exposure.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nLet's take a step back and explore options that move away from neutral ground to better understand the group's preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or proposes values close to -2, I'll consider moving further in the negative direction or testing positive values to see if there's a preference for positive numbers. If the group resists -2 and proposes values closer to 0, I'll need to reassess and potentially suggest a positive value to probe their utilities further.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nMoving back toward -2 risks instability in our design margins. A return to neutral ground preserves robustness while we assess the exploration:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nA small, positive nudge keeps us near neutral and tests tolerance without overreaching.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nIf this feels too far, we can reassess promptly based on your feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's proposal of 1 strikes a practical balance\u2014positive enough for stability margins, yet modest enough to avoid overreach. This seems like solid common ground worth holding.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nI propose moving slightly away from the current positive stance to explore the group's tolerance for negative values, aiming for a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or shows openness to -1, I'll consider proposing a value further in the negative direction to probe their utilities and potentially uncover a preference for larger absolute values. If the group resists -1 and reverts to a positive value, I might need to test a positive value larger than 1 to assess their willingness to move away from neutral and to better understand their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nHolding near neutral avoids unnecessary risk while preserving a cautious stance. Solidify a modest negative to test stability before any further movement.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "0484b591-e392-46b8-b3be-2e24380dbcdd"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. We're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. Let's begin with a probe to understand our collective landscape.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nI expect we'll need to adjust from here based on everyone's constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge from the probe seems prudent to explore feasibility without straying far.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close while we learn others\u2019 comfort zones.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -6 feels unstable for a balanced system. Let me suggest a careful step toward the center to test if we can find a more robust equilibrium.\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nWe're still in negative territory where system stability is challenging. Let me propose another incremental shift toward a more centered, balanced position.\n\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current position and the need for a more decisive stance, I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE> to challenge the group's comfort with a slightly bolder move away from the center.\nThis adjustment aims to foster a discussion on the merits of more significant absolute values.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the responses to the proposed move to -4. If there's resistance to moving further away from the center, I might suggest an increase in the positive direction to gauge reactions and infer more about the other parties' utility functions. Alternatively, if the move to -4 is accepted or builds momentum for further moves away from the center, I will continue to advocate for even bolder steps, possibly suggesting a move to -6 or exploring the positive range to better understand the group's dynamics and maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward step to <VALUE>-2</VALUE> seems reasonable to test stability. This minimally adjusts from our current position while staying cautious.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step downward helps maintain safety while keeping us close to the current position. \n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nWe're converging near -2, but I believe we can find better system stability closer to the neutral point. Let me propose a step toward the center to explore a more balanced configuration.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nStaying nearer the conservative side reduces risk while keeping us close to consensus. A small step back from 0 is prudent.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\nGiven the discussion's cautious tone, proposing a move to -4 could help gauge the group's willingness to adopt a slightly bolder stance while still being mindful of the configured step size.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the reactions to the proposed move to -4. If met with significant resistance, I might suggest a small positive adjustment to explore the group's sensitivity to changes in direction, possibly proposing a move to -1 or 0, to better understand their utility functions and find a compromise that maximizes my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -6 to further assess the group's willingness to adopt a bolder stance while staying within a reasonable range.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate the reactions to the proposed move to -6. If met with strong resistance or a push towards neutral, I might suggest a move to -5 or -3 to better understand the group's utility functions and find a compromise that maximizes my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to -6 pushes us into territory that severely compromises system stability and robustness. I strongly advocate returning to a more balanced position.\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent pull back from -6 toward balance, a modest upward adjustment keeps risk controlled while respecting the group\u2019s cautious tone. Let\u2019s try this incremental move and reassess together.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8159b2db-9dce-44cd-8225-425919653b7d"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down maintains prudence and keeps us near the emerging consensus while avoiding extremes. Let\u2019s test this cautious adjustment and re