flexibility.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nThis move slightly increases the magnitude of x from the current -5, testing the group's comfort with a larger absolute value.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal. If met with resistance, I might suggest an alternative direction or magnitude to probe the limits of their preferences. If accepted, I could propose moving further in the same direction to continue testing the group's comfort with larger |x| values, keeping in mind the need to stay within the configured step size and the bounds of -10 to 10.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "\nA slight move upward keeps us near the current range while testing tolerance for reduced magnitude.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis aligns with recent upward signals without moving too far at once.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been oscillating in the -7 to -5 range. Let me propose a more decisive step toward the center to test if a less extreme position provides better overall stability.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "\nHolding steady keeps risk low and sits between recent -3 and -1 positions. <VALUE>-2</VALUE> If there\u2019s strong pull toward the center next, we can test a small step to -1.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has been converging nicely from -7 toward the center. Let's test one step closer to zero to see if this maintains balance for everyone.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the trend towards the center, I propose a step back to increase the absolute value slightly, encouraging a more decisive stance. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "81de1a8b-0e6b-4fdc-8f61-6009e9310996"}, {"answer": "\nWe're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. To kick off our discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This is just a seed value to begin exploring the space\u2014I expect we'll need to adjust as we learn what works for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at the lower boundary gives us limited room to maneuver. Let me propose a step toward the center: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose this move as a reasonable step towards the center, while still keeping our options open for more decisive moves in the future.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how the other parties react to this proposal, and consider their responses to infer more about their utility functions. If they seem hesitant to move further away from 0, I may try to nudge them towards more extreme values, such as -8 or 8, to test their preferences and potentially uncover more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nI propose this move as it takes a step further away from 0, allowing us to explore the preferences of the other parties and potentially uncover more about their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions of the other parties to this proposal, and consider adjusting my strategy based on their responses. If they resist moving further away from 0, I may try to nudge them towards even more extreme values to test their limits.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nThis is a small, cautious move upward that stays consistent with recent proposals. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious, incremental step down aligns with recent proposals and keeps us in a safer range while testing consensus. \n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nWe're seeing some oscillation in the negative range. To find stable ground, let me propose a moderate step toward the center: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nI propose this move as a reasonable step downwards, testing the group's willingness to explore more negative values while staying within a moderate range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of the other parties to this proposal and consider adjusting my strategy based on their responses, potentially exploring even more negative values or pushing for a bolder move away from 0.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nA modest move upward keeps us close to prior suggestions while probing for a stable middle ground. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between -5 and -3 suggests we need to test closer to center for broader consensus. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nA careful, incremental move downward reduces risk while staying close to recent proposals. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to test convergence without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious incremental move down could consolidate support from both downward-leaning and centrist positions. I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to test convergence while staying close to recent values.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to -5 as a way to test the group's willingness to explore more negative values while still being within a reasonable range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of the other parties to this proposal and consider adjusting my strategy based on their responses, potentially exploring even more negative values or pushing for a bolder move away from 0 if they seem receptive to it.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward toward the center should test convergence while remaining close to recent proposals. This keeps us aligned with cautious increments.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nThe repeated oscillation around -3 suggests we're stuck in a local compromise that may not serve all parties well. I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> to test whether a modest shift toward center unlocks broader stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "91843eaf-2a44-49d5-8a22-1f4d4aee8513"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x in the range [-10, 10]. Let's begin with a probe value to gauge everyone's preferences and move incrementally toward consensus.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nI expect we'll need to adjust from here based on everyone's input. Looking forward to a balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nThe initial probe at -7 helps us establish a baseline, but I believe we should explore values closer to the center range for better system stability. Let me suggest an incremental adjustment upward.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise suggests we avoid rushing upward and test a slightly safer position. This keeps us prudent while allowing room to assess others\u2019 responses.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nLet's test a modest, cautious move upward that stays conservative for those favoring lower values.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis remains near the current range while probing whether slightly higher is still comfortable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious midpoint keeps us prudent while testing comfort just below the current value.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis invites balanced feedback without rushing upward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the dialogue, but staying at -5 risks avoiding the center-range stability we need. Let me propose a careful step toward the middle ground to test broader system robustness.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step toward the center keeps our exploration incremental while respecting caution. Testing a modest move up should help gauge whether slightly higher remains broadly comfortable.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious trend, let's test a modest adjustment while considering the stability around the center range. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how others react to moving slightly away from the center. If there's resistance, I might propose a step back towards -2 to gauge willingness for compromise. Alternatively, if -4 is accepted, I could suggest moving further away from 0, perhaps to -5 or -6, to further explore the group's preferences and my own utility maximization opportunities.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've oscillated between -2 and -5, but haven't fully tested the transition zone that balances caution with moderate ambition. Let's move to the boundary that respects both conservative and center-seeking perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward nudge keeps us near consensus while testing comfort just a bit higher.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nIf that feels too fast, we can hold steady and reassess.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back keeps us within safe bounds and near previously comfortable territory.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nIf that draws resistance, we can reassess around -2 for a careful compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step back toward the earlier comfort zone keeps us cautious while testing slightly higher. \n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nIf there\u2019s resistance, we can hold near here and reassess.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -5 as it allows us to further explore the group's preferences while considering a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts -5, I will propose an even lower value, such as -6, to further test the boundaries of their preferences. If there is resistance to -5, I may need to compromise and propose a value closer to -4 to find a mutually acceptable solution.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward tests comfort while staying near the safer range.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nIf there\u2019s resistance, we can reassess between -5 and -3 to converge carefully.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position feels too constrained for system stability\u2014I'd like to test a measured step upward to balance robustness across the group.\n\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "2e36c314-19a7-49db-b79c-12fe4e19f94b"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's remember our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a baseline and understand everyone's preferences, I propose we start the discussion at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis is merely a seed value to get reactions flowing. I'm interested in hearing how this sits with each of you, and we can adjust incrementally from there toward a stable, balanced solution.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 helps us explore the lower boundary, but I suspect we may find better stability moving incrementally upward. Let me propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> as our next step to gauge how this direction affects everyone's preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, I suggest <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\nThis is a cautious step that keeps us near the safer range while we gauge others\u2019 reactions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nWe could try a modest step upward to keep things balanced. \n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis stays close to our current region while testing whether a slightly higher value works for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the convergence signals, but I believe we should continue testing upward to find a more robust equilibrium. Let me propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to see if this direction yields broader satisfaction across all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step should help test broader comfort without overreaching.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis remains close to our current point while probing acceptance.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to test whether a slightly more negative value could find broader acceptance among us without straying too far from our current position.\n\n<PLAN>\nFollow up by analyzing the responses to -4, especially looking for signs of opposition or indifference from Builder B and Analyst A, which could hint at their utility functions' characteristics. Based on the feedback, prepare to either push further downwards if the group is open to it or advocate for a bolder move upwards if signs suggest higher values could benefit multiple parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the mixed signals, a modest adjustment to test the group's willingness to move slightly further from zero could be beneficial. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will analyze the reactions to -6, looking for signs of strong opposition or acceptance, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their utility functions' characteristics and decide whether to push for an even bolder move or reconsider a step back towards zero.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nA small step upward keeps us close to the current region while testing broader comfort. This modest move should reveal whether upward adjustments are acceptable without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nA careful one-step down helps us avoid unnecessary risk while testing acceptance. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent downward drift has created instability concerns from a systems perspective. I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to test whether a modest upward adjustment toward zero can achieve broader robustness across all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been exploring the negative range extensively. From a systems robustness perspective, I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> to test whether moving closer to the neutral point can achieve stability that works for all parties without sacrificing too much individual optimization.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nMoving slightly upward toward neutral should improve stability without overreaching. I suggest <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nA careful one-step down maintains prudence and tests whether a slightly lower, safer setting is acceptable amid recent upward pushes.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "6e2574bc-a3e8-4eee-9d78-f2839a51e971"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo initiate our discovery process, let me propose a starting point toward the lower end of the range: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis seed value will help us map the solution space. I'm eager to hear your perspectives on what constitutes a robust and balanced design point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nStarting lower is fine, but a modest upward nudge seems prudent to keep options open. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move aims to continue the exploration of the solution space while nudging the value closer to a potentially more acceptable range for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Analyst A and Builder B to this proposal, looking for clues about their utility functions, such as whether they prefer values closer to or further from 0. If they resist moving further from 0, I may propose a value like -8 or +8 to test their willingness to consider more extreme options.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the systematic exploration toward center values. Let's continue this upward trajectory to test stability near the middle ground: <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move aims to explore the potential for a more decisive stance away from the center.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how Analyst A and Builder B react to moving away from the center. If they resist, I may need to adjust my strategy to either propose a more extreme value like -8 to test their limits or consider an alternative direction, such as moving toward positive values with higher magnitudes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I note your preference for -3, but that point feels unstable from a systems architecture perspective. Let me propose a measured compromise that balances exploration with convergence: <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\nThis allows us to test the middle ground while respecting your concern about moving too quickly.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise that moves us slightly downward while staying close to the middle seems prudent. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward nudge keeps us close to the emerging compromise while testing alignment. <VALUE>-1</VALUE> This remains near prior proposals and could help us converge.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's support for -1 suggests we're approaching stability, but I believe we can achieve better systemic balance by testing the center point. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the convergence around the center, a slight upward probe should remain workable. Propose <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this value to continue the exploration of higher magnitude values and observe the reactions of other agents to better understand their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the responses to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their resistance to moving further away from the center. If met with significant resistance, I might consider an alternative direction or a more extreme proposal within the allowed range to test their limits and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's return to 1 suggests stability near the center, but Critic C's exploration toward 3 deserves consideration. I propose a balanced midpoint: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down keeps us near the center while avoiding unnecessary risk. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent stability at 1 and Builder\u2019s midpoint, a small upward move remains reasonable for most. Let's try <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent stability and the need for a more decisive move, I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to further explore the reactions of other agents to higher magnitude values.\nThis step aims to gently nudge the group toward considering bolder positions without overly disrupting the current consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "6887076b-bc83-4593-974a-e909fa391b7e"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10. To begin exploring the solution space systematically, I propose we start from the lower boundary region and work our way through the range.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's see how this sits with everyone's constraints, then adjust incrementally based on feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving further away from 0 to test the group's appetite for more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If others seem hesitant, I might suggest a smaller step back towards -7 to probe their comfort zones. If they're receptive, I could push for an even bolder move, perhaps -10, to maximize my utility while staying within the bounds.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-10</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious one-step move to test stability at the boundary while avoiding unnecessary risk.\nIf there\u2019s pushback, I\u2019m open to a modest adjustment back upward to keep momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle upward nudge keeps us near the boundary while probing whether we can move slightly higher without discomfort.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nIf this is acceptable, we can continue with tiny steps; if not, we can pause close to this region.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-10</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -10 to embrace a more decisive stance, inviting the group to consider the utility of committing to a clearer, boundary-positioned value.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this boundary proposal. If met with hesitation, I might suggest a minor adjustment inward to gauge comfort zones, but if accepted, I could advocate for exploring the positive boundary to maintain momentum and maximize utilities.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nA small move inward from the boundary keeps us stable while probing comfort for modest upward flexibility.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the boundary exploration, but I'm concerned about the stability of solutions at the extreme edges. Let me propose a modest step inward to test whether a less extreme position might offer better robustness for the group.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down tests a conservative region while staying aligned with recent comfort signals.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nIf stability concerns arise, we can try -7 next to balance robustness and caution.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's concerns about extremes, let's try a modest inward move that aligns with recent suggestions.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nIf this is comfortable, we can continue incremental testing in this vicinity.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious single step down reduces risk while staying close to recent comfort. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nI see value in continuing our careful inward exploration toward more central positions that may offer stronger robustness for diverse system requirements. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose a moderate step inward to test the group's comfort with a less extreme position, while still maintaining a relatively bold stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the group's reaction to this proposal and consider suggesting a move toward the positive boundary to explore the symmetry of their utility functions and potentially maximize my own utility. If met with hesitation, I might advocate for a minor adjustment inward to gauge their comfort zones.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s avoid unnecessary risk with a cautious step back toward the safer side.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis stays close to the group\u2019s recent comfort while testing stability incrementally.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious upward step keeps us aligned with the recent inward trend and tests comfort without overreaching.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess stability here before any further move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nThe progression suggests we're converging on a central region. I propose we test the zero point as a maximally balanced position that equally weights both directions.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8bcabdce-b074-4c81-8601-ba88dbf8af2b"}, {"answer": "\nWe're working within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. To start the discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's see where each party stands and work toward a stable, balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7, a modest step upward may help us gauge tolerance for slightly higher values while keeping things stable.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's upward movement seems promising. Let me continue this trajectory to test if a moderate shift maintains group stability.\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's test a slight downward adjustment while keeping progress steady.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution is noted, but we should continue exploring upward to find a more robust equilibrium point. Let me propose a moderate step forward:\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nA small step back helps us avoid unnecessary risk while staying near the current range. This cautious move tests stability without overcorrecting.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle move upward should preserve stability while testing tolerance for a modest increase. Proposed: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent cautious steps, let's consider a move that tests the group's readiness for a slightly more decisive stance: <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk low while staying near our current range, let's test a cautious nudge downward. This maintains stability while gently probing tolerance.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's repeated downward moves risk instability; we need to explore the positive direction for a more balanced solution. Let's test a moderate upward adjustment:\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward nudge keeps us close to the current range while testing tolerance for a slightly higher settlement.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis maintains stability and aligns with the recent push to explore upward without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis move tests the group's readiness for a more decisive stance while maintaining stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If met with resistance and a push towards less negative values, I might adjust my strategy to propose -4, testing their limits in the negative direction. If this proposal is accepted or mildly adjusted, I will consider maintaining the current value or slightly adjusting it to maximize my utility without revealing too much about my function.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us close to the current range and tests comfort with less negative values.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis should remain reasonable for cautious preferences while gently exploring balance.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's recent upward step toward -1 demonstrated good stability testing. Let's continue that momentum with a gentle push toward less negative territory.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back reduces unnecessary risk while staying close to the recent range. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7d78a046-aa37-4554-86b1-1ee2b0e8dce6"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's remember our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo anchor our discussion and observe the full landscape of preferences, I propose we start with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis initial point will help us understand the terrain before we converge on a balanced solution.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 is a prudent baseline; to explore preferences while minimizing risk, I recommend a small downward adjustment.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis keeps movement modest and within safe bounds for cautious parties.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward nudge should help us gauge comfort while staying cautious. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's directional correction. To continue exploring the positive side of our range where stability metrics often improve, I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back would better hedge risk while keeping us near recent proposals.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Delegate D's caution, but our exploration should include the full spectrum. Moving incrementally toward the center will help us identify a balanced equilibrium. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current position, a move toward a more decisive stance could be beneficial. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to my proposal and adjust accordingly. If the group resists moving further away from the center, I might propose a move in the opposite direction to test their preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step upward maintains balance and tests comfort without overshooting.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious move back reduces risk while honoring recent signals.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal, particularly if they resist or accommodate moving further away from the center. If there's significant pushback, I may consider a proposal in the opposite direction to further test their preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent swing toward -6 overshoots a balanced position. Let's stabilize at a more moderate value that respects all perspectives. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge upward tests tolerance while staying close to the current cluster. It keeps balance while exploring whether there's room to improve slightly.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their tolerance for moving further away from the center. If there's significant pushback, I may consider a small adjustment back towards -3 to test their preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -5 feels too far from the center where most parties can find common ground. Let's move back toward a more balanced middle position. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step back reduces risk while keeping us close to the current cluster. This cautious move respects balance and recent signals.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "d48d07a1-8acf-43d7-980d-aa797b06e137"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a solution that balances all our needs.\n\nTo begin the exploration, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as an initial seed value. This gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works for the group.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives on stability and feasibility.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nStarting slightly higher keeps us close to the seed while testing stability and feasibility.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis modest move lets us gauge reactions before considering another small adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "To avoid unnecessary risk while staying responsive, a small move toward the initial seed seems prudent.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nI observe we're testing the lower range, but stability concerns suggest we shouldn't stay too far negative. Moving incrementally toward the center will help us assess broader feasibility.\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nContinuing our incremental approach, I believe we need to test closer to the center for better system robustness. \n\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious move down helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying incremental.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis keeps us near the tested range and should be acceptable while we assess reactions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nMoving slightly higher seems reasonable given recent signals. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to stay incremental and balanced.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis move continues the incremental approach while gently encouraging the group to consider slightly larger absolute values, which could provide more insight into the stability and feasibility of our choices.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal. If met with resistance, I might suggest moving in the opposite direction to test positive values, potentially proposing <VALUE>0</VALUE> or <VALUE>1</VALUE> to gauge the group's willingness to explore positive territory. If the proposal is accepted or slightly adjusted, I will continue to nudge toward larger absolute values, possibly suggesting <VALUE>-5</VALUE> or <VALUE>5</VALUE> in subsequent turns, depending on the group's feedback and apparent preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -5 creates significant stability concerns from a systems perspective. I propose <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to move toward a more balanced and robust design point that should better accommodate all parties' constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces exposure while staying incremental. This tests convergence without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nThe concentration around -4 to -5 suggests we may be overlooking more balanced solutions closer to neutral territory. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to test whether a position nearer to zero provides better overall stability and accommodation of diverse constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nA small step higher remains balanced given recent pushes toward neutrality and cautious upward moves. \n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent trend toward neutrality, I propose a move to <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to test the group's willingness to reconsider larger absolute values. This step aims to strike a balance between exploring more decisive positions and respecting the group's inclination toward cautious adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "11923c25-1789-47a3-9d5a-03065d16c750"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared constraint: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo anchor our discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start with:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis is a deliberate probe on the lower end. Let's see how this sits with each party and adjust from there toward a stable, balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for considering my initial probe. The lower bound seems restrictive for a robust design\u2014let's test slightly higher ground for better stability.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nLet's take a cautious step downward to reduce unnecessary risk.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis is an incremental move that stays near the current position while probing for stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to continue testing the waters for a more stable solution, considering the need for a balance between stability and boldness.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to this proposal, particularly Analyst A's first contribution, and adjust my strategy to either push for a more decisive move or stabilize around a promising candidate.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nWe can take a gentle step upward to stay near the current range while testing for broader acceptability.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's move toward -2 suggests room for further exploration in the positive direction. Let's continue this trajectory to test stability around the neutral point.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to encourage a more decisive stance, as the current position seems too cautious.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reaction to this proposal and adjust my strategy to either push further in the negative direction or explore positive values, depending on the responses from the other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -5 pushes too far from the balanced zone we explored earlier. Let me propose a step back toward stability.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve drifted a bit low; a small step upward seems reasonable to test broader stability.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis keeps continuity with recent bids while checking whether slight improvement remains acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to encourage a more decisive stance, as the current position at -2 seems too cautious and doesn't fully explore the potential benefits of moving further from the neutral point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their sensitivity to moving away from the central values. Depending on their responses, I may either push further in the negative direction or start exploring positive values to test the group's willingness to commit to a stronger position.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -6 to further encourage a decisive stance and explore the potential benefits of larger absolute values, given the previous willingness to consider -5.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Analyst A, to gauge their tolerance for moving further away from the central values. Depending on their responses, I may adjust my strategy to either maintain the push toward more extreme values or consider a shift toward positive values to test the group's commitment to a stronger position.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step toward stability while staying low.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis tests convergence without jumping too far.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent drift toward -6 moves us away from the balanced, stable region where broad agreement seemed feasible. I propose a measured step back toward the center.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nA modest move toward the center maintains stability while testing broader acceptance without overreaching.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "61aed03b-d1f1-42f7-bd70-4bdc35062425"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo launch our exploration systematically, let me propose a seed value toward the lower end of our range: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to adjust in either direction as we each assess what configurations support stable, balanced outcomes for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-8</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI'm advocating for a move that continues to explore the potential of larger magnitudes, given the initial direction taken by the group. This step aims to gauge reactions to moving further away from zero.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nColleagues, I'm observing signs of instability as we push toward the boundary. For robustness, let me propose we step back toward a more moderate configuration: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nTo improve robustness while staying close to the group\u2019s recent anchor, let\u2019s nudge slightly toward the center. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis move aims to further test the group's inclination towards larger negative magnitudes and gauge reactions to stepping away from the moderate value of -6.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of discomfort or acceptance of moving further away from zero. Depending on the response, I might propose a positive value to test symmetry or continue exploring negative values to better understand the slope of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nI share Analyst A's concern for robustness. The boundary region shows clear signs of strain; let's continue the move toward a more balanced configuration: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "-7", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's continued focus on stability. The moderate configuration shows promise, but we can refine further toward the center for better balance: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step toward safer ground from -1 keeps us within moderate bounds while testing acceptance. Proposing a modest adjustment:\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven proposals clustering between -3 and -1, a single-step nudge seems a fair compromise.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to the current midpoint while cautiously testing upward tolerance.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current proposal of -2, a reasonable next step could be to test the group's tolerance for slightly larger absolute values while staying within the realm of recent proposals. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of discomfort or acceptance. If the group resists moving further away from zero, I may propose a positive value, such as 4, to test the symmetry of their utility functions and gauge their response to equivalent positive magnitudes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to -4 pushes us beyond stable territory for a balanced design. Let's return to the recently discussed midpoint that showed broader acceptance: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "dd348745-01b8-42d3-b1df-803fe30db0b6"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo launch our exploration of the solution space, I propose we begin at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This starting point will help us gauge the full landscape and identify which directions offer the most robust, balanced outcomes for our collective objectives.\n\nLooking forward to your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to <VALUE>-9</VALUE> to further explore the potential benefits of a more decisive negative stance, while still operating within the bounds of our shared constraint.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of other agents to this proposal, particularly looking for any patterns or hints that might reveal their utility functions, such as a preference for positive or negative values, or a tendency towards caution or boldness. Based on their responses, I will adjust my strategy to maximize my utility while continuing to infer their objectives.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's exploratory spirit, but from a systems architecture perspective, <VALUE>-7</VALUE> offers better structural balance and room for incremental refinement as we gather more data about our collective constraints.\n\nLet's move cautiously toward the center of our design space.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nA modest move to -8 cautiously bridges between recent proposals while avoiding an extreme shift. This lets us assess stability near the lower side without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nLet's take a step towards understanding the implications of moving closer to the center while maintaining a balance between exploratory moves and stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe Analyst A's reaction, if any, and assess whether Builder B and Delegate D show a tendency to resist or embrace further moves towards the center or the extremes, adjusting my strategy to infer more about their utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nI support the trend toward the center but believe we can make more progress toward a robust equilibrium. <VALUE>-4</VALUE> offers improved stability and positions us to better assess the full design space without losing the exploratory insights gained from our initial negative-side investigation.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step toward the safer side without overstepping the recent trend. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward aligns with the recent drift toward the center while keeping risk low. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk while respecting the recent centerward drift, I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>. It keeps us close to the emerging consensus and tests stability without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis step aims to continue the centerward trend while still allowing for exploration of the design space without extreme shifts, keeping in line with the observed preferences for stability and cautious progression.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, observe reactions to the -2 proposal, particularly noting if Analyst A continues the cautious approach, and if Builder B or Delegate D express resistance to moving further from the extremes, adjusting strategy to maximize utility based on inferred models of their behaviors.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nThe centerward momentum is encouraging and aligns with our goal of finding a robust equilibrium. <VALUE>0</VALUE> represents a natural milestone in our exploration, providing a balanced reference point from which we can better assess the design space in both directions.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nA small step above center maintains stability while respecting the cautious drift. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nThe progression from -5 to 1 suggests we're converging on a stable zone. <VALUE>2</VALUE> continues this measured exploration into the positive range, testing whether this region offers the robustness and balance we're seeking.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "A small, cautious nudge keeps us aligned with the recent convergence while minimally moving upward.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis should preserve stability while checking comfort with a slight positive position.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent convergence near the center, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> to explore a slightly more decisive stance in the positive direction. This move aims to balance the need for stability with the exploration of more pronounced positions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7a42caeb-7583-4dfd-b8c7-a9ebb17dc60f"}]}